# Agent Skill Orchestration

For high-cost or ambiguous work, use an explicit chain instead of responding in one hop.

## Quick Router

- unclear request -> `superpowers-brainstorming`
- explicit plan request -> `superpowers-writing-plans`
- "review my plan" / "what am I missing" -> `grill-me`
- debugging / instability -> `superpowers-systematic-debugging`
- repo understanding -> `dl-vision-repo-workflow`
- paper to implementation -> `paper-lookup` + `literature-review` + `dl-vision-paper-to-code`
- training / extraction command work -> `ace-training-command-composer` or `ace-memory-extraction-workflow`
- results / benchmark comparison -> `ace-result-aggregation` + `dl-vision-experiment-reporting`

Then add:

- `grill-me` before locking important decisions
- `karpathy` during implementation tightening
- verification skills before completion

## Default Chains

### Clarify -> Plan -> Critique

Use when requirements are unclear or there are multiple plausible solutions:

- `superpowers-using-superpowers`
- `superpowers-brainstorming`
- `superpowers-writing-plans`
- `grill-me`
- `karpathy`

### Retrieve -> Synthesize -> Challenge

Use when the task needs strong evidence or technical synthesis:

- `dl-vision-repo-workflow`
- `paper-lookup`
- `literature-review`
- `dl-vision-paper-to-code`
- `grill-me`
- `karpathy`

### Experiment Work

Use when building or evaluating training / memory / benchmark runs:

- `dl-vision-experiment-orchestration`
- `dl-vision-benchmark-alignment`
- `dl-vision-experiment-reporting`
- `ace-training-command-composer` or `ace-memory-extraction-workflow`
- `grill-me`

### Debugging

Use when isolating failures:

- `superpowers-systematic-debugging`
- `dl-vision-training-failure-triage`
- `dl-vision-checkpoint-resume-integrity`
- `dl-vision-gpu-performance`
- `superpowers-verification-before-completion`
- `karpathy`

## Repo-Specific Pairings

- memory extraction: `ace-memory-extraction-workflow` -> `grill-me` -> `karpathy`
- training commands: `ace-training-command-composer` -> `dl-vision-experiment-orchestration` -> `grill-me`
- result synthesis: `ace-result-aggregation` -> `dl-vision-experiment-reporting` -> `dl-vision-benchmark-alignment`
- runbook decisions: `ace-scene-runbook` -> `grill-me` -> `karpathy`

## Rule

If a weak answer would waste GPU time, engineering effort, or research cycles, use a chain, not a single skill.
